---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Final from '../components/Final.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site.js';

const seo = {
  title: 'About Alister Gates | Executive Coach, IFS-Trained, 35 Years in Business',
  description: 'Alister Gates spent 35 years in business before training as a counsellor and in Internal Family Systems. He now coaches founders and senior leaders online, from Zurich.',
};
const credentials = [
  '35 years as an entrepreneur: IT and software, export, product development, marketing',
  'CTO of a software company in the early 2000s; helped raise over $10 million',
  'Built and sold several businesses, mainly in FMCG, food and health',
  'Internal Family Systems (IFS) Level 2 trained',
  'Bachelor of Applied Counselling',
  'Certified Nice Guy Coach with Dr Robert Glover',
  'Couples training in Intimacy from the Inside Out (IFIO) and the Developmental Model',
  "Men's work facilitator with the Mankind Project since 2005",
];
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE}/#person`, '@type': 'Person', name: 'Alister Gates', url: `${SITE}/about/`, image: `${SITE}/images/alister-office.jpg`, sameAs: ['https://alistergates.com/about/', 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/alistergates/'] },
};
---
<Base title={seo.title} description={seo.description} schema={schema} image="/images/alister-office.jpg">
  <section class="on-dark">
    <div class="wrap section ab-hero">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="label">About</p>
        <h1 class="h1">I came to this work <em>the long way round.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">Thirty-five years in business, then a counselling degree, then Internal Family Systems. I'm Alister Gates. I coach leaders who are good at their jobs and tired of how much it's costing them.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ab-photo"><img src="/images/alister-office.webp" width="896" height="1088" alt="Alister Gates" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">01 — The business years</p><h2 class="h2">I know what it's like <em>to carry it.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p>At 25 I bought my first business, a computer shop. From 1992 to 2006 I worked in tech, patenting software and selling it internationally. In the early 2000s I was CTO of a software company, smart software built to do work that lawyers did, an early cousin of today's AI. I helped raise over $10 million for it, and I was the one selling the tech story to investors. It was ahead of its time, and the people we were selling to didn't much like it. The company struggled until we did the one thing that turned it round: we moved into the market we were selling to and turned up in front of customers. After tech, I built and sold several businesses, mostly in FMCG, food and health.</p>
        <p>I've helped raise capital, built and sold businesses, employed people, made payroll, taken risks that kept me up at night, had wins and had failures. I know the particular loneliness of being the person everyone looks to when you're not sure of the answer yourself.</p>
        <p>I also know how easy it is to build something impressive on the outside while avoiding everything on the inside. I was good at it. Most of the leaders I work with are too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tone-stone">
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">02 — The turn</p><h2 class="h2">More interested in the person <em>than the product.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p>There wasn't a dramatic breakdown, just a slow realisation. I'd been running men's circles with the Mankind Project since 2005, and I kept seeing what happens when capable people drop the performance and tell the truth. That interested me more than anything I was selling.</p>
        <p>So I retrained formally as a counsellor. Then I found Internal Family Systems, and it explained what I'd watched for decades in boardrooms and in myself. People don't keep repeating patterns because they're stupid or weak. They do it because a part of them is working very hard to protect them.</p>
        <p>Today I work as a couples and individual counsellor at <a href="https://alistergates.com/">alistergates.com</a>, and with leaders here. The two overlap more than you'd think. The pattern that runs the leadership team usually runs the marriage too.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">03 — Between cultures</p><h2 class="h2">Leading a long way <em>from home.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p>My father was a diplomat. By 14 I'd lived in London, New York, New Zealand, Samoa, Fiji and Tonga, and later I spent four years in Tokyo. I'm now based in Zurich.</p>
        <p>That kind of life makes you adaptable and good at reading a room. It can also leave you slightly untethered, able to fit in anywhere and not quite sure where you belong. Many of the expat executives I work with recognise that straight away.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tone-stone">
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <div class="stack"><p class="label">04 — Training</p><h2 class="h2">Background <em>and credentials.</em></h2></div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <ul class="rules creds">{credentials.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}</ul>
        <p class="small">This work is IFS-informed. I'm trained in Internal Family Systems, but I'm not affiliated with or endorsed by the IFS Institute.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Final heading="If any of this sounds familiar," em="let's talk." text="Twenty minutes, no pitch. You'll know quickly whether we're a fit." image="old-pier" />
</Base>

<style>
  .ab-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 4fr); gap: 40px 72px; align-items: center; }
  .ab-photo { margin: 0; }
  .ab-photo img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 20%; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .ab-hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .ab-photo { max-width: 360px; } }
  .creds li { border-color: var(--stone-rule) !important; }
  .small { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted-2); }
</style>
